---
Title: Code that throws
---

<script data-type="jmarkdown">
function shout(s) { return s.toUpperCase(); }
export_to_jmarkdown('shout');
</script>

A simple function runs: shout(hello there). Given a double quote, its call is
not valid JavaScript: shout(he said "hi").

<script data-type="jmarkdown">
throw new Error('script boom');
</script>

<script data-type="jmarkdown-postprocess">
throw new Error('postprocess boom');
</script>

After the errors, the build carries on.
